{"dossier":"D15","entry_points":[{"sids":["fs/fhandle.c::sys_open_by_handle_at","fs/fhandle.c::compat_sys_open_by_handle_at","fs/fhandle.c::do_handle_open"],"text":"Open-by-handle resolves mount plus handle plus flags to a path, opens and installs with large-file forced natively."},{"sids":["fs/file.c::last_fd","fs/file.c::__range_cloexec","fs/file.c::__range_close","fs/file.c::sys_close_range"],"text":"Range ops clamp to the live top and resample after lock drops. Entry validates, optionally privatizes, applies and installs. Unshare duplicates omitting the range unless cloexec-only preserves it, then swaps."},{"sids":["fs/file_table.c::proc_nr_files","fs/file_table.c::fs_stat_sysctls","fs/file_table.c::init_fs_stat_sysctls","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::register_sysctl_mount_point","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::register_sysctl_sz"],"text":"Boot publishes file counts with on-demand summation and optional mount reservation; in-use is read-only with bounded maxima."}],"exports":[{"sids":["fs/namei.c::filename_lookup","fs/open.c::file_open_root","fs/namei.c::do_file_open_root","fs/nsfs.c::nsfs_get_root","fs/pidfs.c::pidfs_get_root"],"text":"Name lookup resolves a prepared name with flags into a path under an optional root and audits success. Anchored open translates mode and retries. Special roots hand out referenced stable paths. Both follow RCU then plain then revalidating attempts; anchored open rejects symlink roots."},{"sids":["fs/locks.c::fcntl_setlk64","fs/fcntl.c::send_sigurg","fs/fcntl.c::send_sigurg_to_task","fs/namespace.c::has_locked_children"],"text":"Range locks cover private and blocking forms with OFD zero-pid, private ownership and 64-bit rewrite. The files spin orders lookup against close, revalidating and dropping POSIX state on races. Urgent delivery samples owner identity under lock with RCU walk. Child scan reports locked mounts under a dentry."},{"sids":["fs/file.c::dup_fd","fs/file.c::close_files","fs/file.c::put_files_struct","fs/file.c::exit_files","fs/file.c::__get_unused_fd_flags","fs/file.c::get_unused_fd_flags","fs/file.c::put_unused_fd","fs/file.c::iterate_fd"],"text":"Duplication copies the live prefix under the source lock into a fresh owner, skipping unpublished slots and publishing by RCU. Teardown closes set bits and frees on last put with exit detach. Allocation scans from zero under a ceiling; release needs the owner lock. Iteration walks present files without references."},{"sids":["fs/file.c::__get_file_rcu","fs/file.c::get_file_rcu","fs/file.c::get_file_active","fs/file.c::fget_raw","fs/file.c::fget_task","fs/file.c::fget_task_next","fs/file.c::receive_fd","include/linux/file.h::fd_prepare_fd","fs/file.c::receive_fd_replace","fs/file.c::ksys_dup3","fs/file.c::sys_dup3","fs/file.c::sys_dup2","fs/file.c::sys_dup"],"text":"Lockless lookup elevates then revalidates pointers, handling recycle and EAGAIN. Task lookup scans under task lock. Receive gates, reserves, elevates, notifies and publishes. Dup checks flags, limits and existence, allows only cloexec, maps faults, and installs with self-check and cleanup."},{"sids":["fs/file_attr.c::vfs_fileattr_set","fs/file_attr.c::fileattr_set_prepare","include/linux/fscrypt.h::fscrypt_prepare_setflags","fs/file_attr.c::vfs_fileattr_get","fs/file_attr.c::ioctl_getflags","fs/file_attr.c::ioctl_setflags","fs/file_attr.c::ioctl_fsgetxattr","fs/file_attr.c::ioctl_fssetxattr","fs/file_attr.c::sys_file_getattr","fs/file_attr.c::sys_file_setattr","fs/namespace.c::mnt_want_write_file","fs/namespace.c::mnt_drop_write_file"],"text":"Attribute set validates against current state with encryption and security checks under exclusive inode ownership, then delegates and notifies. Project, immutable and hint rules are type and namespace gated with family carryover. User calls translate forms, accept limited flags with size checks, and hold ordered mount write protection."}],"extracts":["4782393d71eb75a87e9144f99cba4de19271c370201f55d4d754f9bd9e1465d7","cdf823e6abd7ea92e29437c9f0256671d2c7efb19faf162332421b41bd6923b8","db61b8d627823f1d9003199d8d3afaaa0beb1990d221845e35fa6a1c40752c5e"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_is_perm_empty_ctl_header","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_set_perm_empty_ctl_header","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_clear_perm_empty_ctl_header","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_print_dir","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::namecmp"],"text":"Duplicates fail with logged context; permanently empty dirs reject inserts and invalid promotions."},{"sids":["include/linux/fortify-string.h::strlen","include/uapi/linux/stat.h::S_ISDIR","include/linux/lockdep.h::lockdep_assert_held.alt_1","include/linux/lockdep.h::lockdep_assert_held.alt_2","include/linux/printk.h::pr_cont","include/linux/rbtree.h::rb_entry","include/linux/slab.h::kzalloc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_inc_not_zero","include/linux/completion.h::init_completion","include/linux/container_of.h::container_of","include/linux/fortify-string.h::memcmp","include/linux/fortify-string.h::memcpy","include/linux/kconfig.h::IS_ENABLED","include/linux/kmemleak.h::kmemleak_not_leak","include/linux/list.h::INIT_HLIST_HEAD","include/linux/list.h::hlist_entry","include/linux/percpu_counter.h::percpu_counter_sum_positive.alt_1"],"text":"External string, lock-check, print, tree, alloc, atomic, completion, container, config, leak, list and counter helpers support these paths."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["fs/fcntl.c::copy_flock_fields","fs/fcntl.c::get_compat_flock","fs/fcntl.c::get_compat_flock64","fs/fcntl.c::put_compat_flock","fs/fcntl.c::put_compat_flock64","fs/fcntl.c::fixup_compat_flock","fs/fcntl.c::do_compat_fcntl64","fs/fcntl.c::convert_fcntl_cmd","fs/fcntl.c::compat_sys_fcntl64","fs/fcntl.c::compat_sys_fcntl","fs/fcntl.c::band_table"],"text":"Ranges share five fields copied with zeroed outputs and width checks; fixup rejects or clamps oversize values. Commands map wide forms to native. Poll bands encode six fixed combinations. Compat dispatch validates then routes width and direction; legacy rejects wide and OFD forms; faults abort."},{"sids":["fs/fhandle.c::do_sys_name_to_handle","fs/fhandle.c::handle_to_path","fs/fhandle.c::may_decode_fh","fs/fhandle.c::vfs_dentry_acceptable","fs/fhandle.c::subtree_unobstructed","fs/fhandle.c::capable_wrt_mount","fs/fcntl.c::fasync_lock","fs/fhandle.c::do_handle_to_path","fs/fhandle.c::sys_name_to_handle_at","include/linux/exportfs.h::exportfs_can_encode_fh","fs/fhandle.c::get_path_anchor","include/linux/exportfs.h::FILEID_USER_FLAGS"],"text":"Handles bound sizes with word scaling and header-only overflow. Decode validates sizes and flags, derives connectable and directory modes, and strips user bits. Global search bypasses checks; otherwise directory-only plus admin or readable unobstructed subtree with ancestor mapping and confinement applies under mount and RCU guards through lookup, encode, anchor, permission and decode stages."},{"sids":["fs/file.c::__file_ref_put","fs/file.c::__file_ref_put_badval","include/linux/file_ref.h::__file_ref_read_raw","fs/file.c::__fget_light","fs/file.c::fdget","fs/file.c::fdget_raw","include/linux/file.h::BORROWED_FD","include/linux/file.h::CLONED_FD","fs/file.c::fdget_pos","fs/file.c::file_needs_f_pos_lock","fs/file.c::file_seek_cur_needs_f_lock","fs/file.c::__f_unlock_pos"],"text":"References move among live, saturated and dead with exclusive final transition; surplus releases warn and restore. Light lookup borrows when exclusive else clones with mode filtering into empty, borrowed or cloned handles encoding release duties. Position locking applies only when atomic or shared iteration requires it."},{"sids":["fs/file.c::__read_mostly","fs/file.c::sysctl_nr_open_min","fs/file.c::__const_min","fs/file.c::sysctl_nr_open_max","fs/file.c::sane_fdtable_size","fs/file.c::BITBIT_NR"],"text":"Open ceiling defaults to one million with word floor and masked maximum. Live size follows the top open bit with defaults and hole rescan. Hint sizing nests bit conversions without shown users."},{"sids":["fs/file_attr.c::fileattr_fill_xflags","fs/file_attr.c::fileattr_fill_flags","fs/file_attr.c::fileattr_to_file_attr","fs/file_attr.c::copy_fsxattr_to_user","fs/file_attr.c::file_attr_to_fileattr","fs/file_attr.c::copy_fsxattr_from_user"],"text":"Nine flag properties mirror with validity. Conversion zeroes, masks and copies size fields, rejecting bad bits and faults distinctly and stripping read-only bits. Kernel keeps dual flags; users see extended flags only."}],"locks":[{"sids":["fs/file.c::file_close_fd","include/linux/fdtable.h::rcu_dereference_check_fdtable"],"text":"Close and release serialize under the owner lock with post-unlock teardown; slot access requires the held lock."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::__register_sysctl_table","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::drop_sysctl_table","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::start_unregistering","fs/proc/inode.c::proc_invalidate_siblings_dcache","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::insert_links","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::new_links","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::get_links","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::xlate_dir","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::find_subdir"],"text":"Sysctl create, insert, lookup and drop hold global spin, releasing to drain users on unregister. Purge uses RCU with grabs. Foreign sets keep placeholder root links created only when missing."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p10","crown":"A","phase":"F5"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::erase_header","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::erase_entry","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_invalidate_dcache"],"text":"Last drop unlinks, drains users, purges dentries, removes links and defers reclaim with parent recursion."}],"structs":[{"sids":["fs/file.c::__free_fdtable","fs/file.c::free_fdtable_rcu","fs/file.c::init_files"],"text":"Tables bundle arrays, bitmaps, capacity and RCU state with split allocators and delayed release. Owners embed storage, cursor, wait, lock and count; the primordial owner self-points with unit count."},{"sids":["fs/file_table.c::backing_file.alt_1","fs/file_table.c::backing_file.anon_1","fs/file_table.c::backing_file_security","fs/file_table.c::files_stat","fs/file_table.c::__ro_after_init.alt_1","fs/file_table.c::filp_cache","fs/file_table.c::__ro_after_init.alt_2","fs/file_table.c::bfilp_cache","fs/file_table.c::__cacheline_aligned_in_smp"],"text":"Backing files embed a file plus path-or-callback union and optional security. Accounting pairs cur-max stats with dedicated caches and per-CPU live counts."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::insert_header","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::insert_entry","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::find_entry","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::init_header","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::list_for_each_table_entry"],"text":"Headers link table slices with entry nodes and directory roots, iterated by index with use and lineage tracking; insertion and lookup need the global spin."}],"stubs":[{"sid":"include/linux/sched/task.h::task_lock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D01"},{"sid":"include/linux/sched/task.h::task_unlock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D01"},{"sid":"include/linux/sched.h::cond_resched","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D01"},{"sid":"include/linux/sched/signal.h::rlimit","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D01"},{"sid":"include/linux/rcupdate.h::rcu_dereference_raw","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D02"},{"sid":"include/linux/rcupdate.h::rcu_read_lock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D02"},{"sid":"include/linux/rcupdate.h::rcu_read_unlock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D02"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::READ_ONCE","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock.h::spin_lock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock.h::spin_unlock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock_rt.h::spin_lock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock_rt.h::spin_unlock","state"